  "body": "TDF's SMTP messages left the application without Date or Message-ID, preventing reliable correlation and leaving these fields outside the provider's DKIM signature. This adds both before submission and logs the same attempt ID without recipient addresses, content or arbitrary exception text. Success is explicitly SMTP acceptance, not inbox delivery.\n\nThe audit also found repeated permanent delivery failures and newsletter-style broadcasts through Webador, whose documented service excludes newsletters. Add a validated, operator-reviewed `SMTP_UNDELIVERABLE_RECIPIENTS` setting that rejects before SMTP, and return 409 for real registered-user broadcasts through Webador while preserving previews and individual transactional flows. Marketing opt-outs must never be placed in the delivery-failure setting.\n\nValidation:\n- Six focused Hspec cases, including 100 QuickCheck examples and rejection before connection.\n- Stack/GHC 9.10.3 typecheck of Email and its dependencies.\n- Six monitor tests: healthy replacement Machine discovery, aligned DMARC results, entity rejection, decompression bounds, private DSN summaries, and continuation after actual encrypted/unsupported-compression ZIP attachments.\n- `npm run verify:formal` and `npm run quality:repo` passed.\n- Three explicitly authorized real Gmail tests all reached INBOX/CATEGORY_PERSONAL with SPF/DKIM/DMARC PASS. The actual app template changed from relay `Junk` to `Neutral`, and the corrected Date/Message-ID are included in DKIM's signed header list. These locally executed template tests used production SMTP; they do not assert a Fly deployment or prove a general reputation change.\n\nNo database migration or provider migration. The reviewed private suppression values are prepared but not yet staged in Fly. A read-only local daily DNS/DSN/DMARC monitor is installed; DMARC reporting was saved in Webador, with propagation still inconsistent and no aggregate reports received yet. Outlook/enterprise placement and the reported spam samples remain unverified. The detailed report documents evidence, limits, rollback and dated follow-up.\n\n",
